[65.018817, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[65.099633, "o", "Starting the lab's authorization server on 127.0.0.1 (hardened setup) ... stopped again at the end\r\n\r\n"]
[65.469389, "o", "1. helpdesk-app asks the server where its doors are:  http://127.0.0.1:34395/.well-known/openid-configuration\r\n      sign-in page /authorize   token desk /token   public keys /jwks\r\n"]
[65.469473, "o", "2. helpdesk-app sends Alice to the server's own sign-in page (with a one-time PKCE challenge)\r\n3. Alice types her password THERE: the app never sees it\r\n"]
[65.497417, "o", "4. the server sends her browser back to the app with a one-time code, valid 60 seconds\r\n5. the app swaps that code (plus the PKCE secret only it knows) for an access token:\r\n"]
[65.497479, "o", "      server log: grant=authorization_code client=helpdesk-app user=alice\r\n"]
[65.497705, "o", "\r\n   access token (919 characters): eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsInR5...g0yrAhJrHN3wRIKsQJPc9YfA\r\n   lives 300 seconds. To decode a token like this one: python3 explore.py token\r\n"]
[65.558988, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m20\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m20\u001b[00m$ "]
[73.210143, "o", "p"]
[73.300035, "o", "y"]
[73.421541, "o", "t"]
[73.556846, "o", "h"]
[73.685038, "o", "o"]
[73.811569, "o", "n"]
[73.92318, "o", "3"]
[74.018211, "o", " "]
[74.191618, "o", "e"]
[74.295111, "o", "x"]
[74.424457, "o", "p"]
[74.563081, "o", "l"]
[74.670206, "o", "o"]
[74.777491, "o", "r"]
[74.914847, "o", "e"]
[75.039947, "o", "."]
[75.134526, "o", "p"]
[75.226768, "o", "y"]
[75.320162, "o", " "]
[75.50297, "o", "t"]
[75.632567, "o", "o"]
[75.725838, "o", "k"]
[75.856554, "o", "e"]
[75.995778, "o", "n"]
[76.46783, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[77.15138, "o", "Alice's access token is three parts with dots between them: header . payload . signature\r\n\r\n   header     eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...ZCI6InRzZy1sYWItMSJ9   (64 characters)\r\n   payload    eyJpc3MiOiJodHRwOi8v...lQGV4YW1wbGUuY29tIn0   (511 characters)\r\n"]
[77.151451, "o", "   signature  6Avc9WrtaY2Bv8nKGmL-...2JpxbuLhOpGayv3gl34A   (342 characters)\r\n\r\nThe first two are base64url: an encoding, not encryption. Anyone holding the token can read them."]
[77.151549, "o", "\r\n\r\nheader:   {\"alg\":\"RS256\",\"typ\":\"at+jwt\",\"kid\":\"tsg-lab-1\"}\r\npayload:\r\n   iss                 http://127.0.0.1:37741                       issuer: who wrote and signed it (the lab's server)\r\n   sub                 u-1001-alice                                 subject: who it is about (Alice's user ID)\r\n   aud                 5 services (below)                           audience: which services may accept it\r\n                       orchestrator-agent, tickets-agent, mail-agent, tickets-api, mail-api\r\n   azp                 helpdesk-app                                 authorized party: the app that asked for it\r\n   scope               openid profile tickets:read mail:send        what it allows (+4 aud:... scopes, see README)\r\n"]
[77.151796, "o", "   iat                 1793374928  (15:42:08 UTC)                   issued at (seconds since 1 Jan 1970)\r\n   exp                 1793375228  (15:47:08 UTC)                   expires at\r\n   jti                 h33xdUP4nDe9Dwfk                             JWT ID: a unique serial number for this token\r\n   preferred_username  alice                                        the user's name (for people, not for decisions)\r\n"]
[77.152126, "o", "   email               alice@example.com                            the user's email\r\n   -> lives 300 seconds\r\n\r\nThe signature: the server signed header + payload with its PRIVATE key. Anyone can check it with\r\nthe PUBLIC key it publishes (/jwks, key ID tsg-lab-1):\r\n"]
[77.152212, "o", "   check the token as issued:          signature OK\r\n   check a copy with tickets:delete:   REJECTED (bad signature)\r\n"]
[77.212468, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m20\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m20\u001b[00m$ "]
